<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinhala Only Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1956</span> · Also known as Official Language Act No. 33 of 1956</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sinhala Only Act, formally the Official Language Act No. 33 of 1956, was passed by the Parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/s-w-r-d-bandaranaike">S. W. R. D. Bandaranaike</a>. It replaced English with Sinhala as the sole official language, excluding Tamil, and many Tamil-speaking public servants lost their posts. It deepened the divide between Sinhalese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamils">Tamils</a> that later fed the Sri Lankan Civil War.</p></div>
